# `last = o.f` in a loop, off an object that is out of sight: behind the look at the cell and the guard of the name the walk runs the getter, here as a copy. The getter writes a variable and then reads a field,
# which wants a look of its own. A look at the loop goes into the copy: behind the write no turn begins again, so it counts on no guess there. It used to count on a read that runs no code: the unit was walked again, and the verifier stopped the build.
# The loop keeps its typed copy: the shape is asked in front of it, the two looks of the access begin the turn again where they fail, and the look at the slot, behind the write, has a closed arm of its own.
# f1 = run, f3 = f
# -- source: half-of-an-accessor-that-writes-is-counted-on-by-the-looks-at-the-loop.ts
